  "description": "BoTorchSampler for OptunaSharp — a native OptunaSharp BaseSampler that drives the real BoTorch (PyTorch + GPyTorch) library in-process via Python.NET (pythonnet). A faithful C# port of optuna_integration's BoTorchSampler glue (sampler protocol + candidates_func selection) whose numerics are direct botorch calls, so it is byte-exact with BoTorch. You pick the acquisition function with the pythonnet-free BoTorchCandidatesFunc enum: LogEI, qEI, qLogEI and qNEI for one objective; qEHVI, EHVI, qNEHVI, qParEGO and qLogEI-ParEGO for several; the knowledge-gradient qKG and qHVKG; constrained optimization through Trial.SetConstraint. Does NOT require the Python optuna_integration package — install only `botorch`. The .NET analog of using optuna_integration.BoTorchSampler, built on OptunaSharp.Interop.pythonnet. Part of the SciSharp STACK.",
  "iconFile": "optunasharp-icon.png",
